From: gt510 <gt510@localhost>
Subject: drm/msm/mdp5: don't keep a restored plane's stale hwpipe after resume

drm_atomic_helper_suspend() snapshots the plane states, then disables
everything; the disabling commit releases each plane's hwpipe (and its
SMP blocks) in the mdp5 global state. The snapshot does not include
that private object, so on drm_atomic_helper_resume() the restored plane
states still point at their old hwpipes while the global state has them
unassigned. mdp5_plane_atomic_check() keeps a plane's hwpipe whenever the
caps fit, so the restored plane scans out of a pipe nobody owns, and the
next commit that releases it trips the WARN in mdp5_pipe_release() and
fails with -EINVAL. On SM-T550 (MSM8916) this happens whenever the
display is on at suspend time (logind suspends on a lid/hall event while
the panel is lit): after resume phoc's DPMS-off commit fails ("Failed to
commit power mode change") and the panel stays on until reboot.

A plane that is not visible in the current state owns no hwpipe, so treat
any hwpipe in its new state as stale and assign the pipes afresh.
---
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/disp/mdp5/mdp5_plane.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/disp/mdp5/mdp5_plane.c
@@ -239,6 +239,22 @@
 
 		if (plane->type == DRM_PLANE_TYPE_CURSOR)
 			caps |= MDP_PIPE_CAP_CURSOR;
+
+		/*
+		 * A plane that is not visible in the current state owns no
+		 * hwpipe. If the new state names one anyway, it was restored
+		 * from a snapshot (drm_atomic_helper_resume() after system
+		 * suspend): the snapshot keeps the plane's hwpipe pointers but
+		 * not the global hwpipe assignment, and the suspend commit
+		 * released the pipes. Keeping such a pipe leaves it unowned in
+		 * the global state, so the next commit that releases it fails
+		 * with -EINVAL and the CRTC can no longer be disabled. Assign
+		 * the pipes afresh instead.
+		 */
+		if (!plane_enabled(old_state)) {
+			mdp5_state->hwpipe = NULL;
+			mdp5_state->r_hwpipe = NULL;
+		}
 
 		/* (re)allocate hw pipe if we don't have one or caps-mismatch: */
 		if (!mdp5_state->hwpipe || (caps & ~mdp5_state->hwpipe->caps))
